# /etc/trend-investing/accounts/trad-ira.env  (root:root, mode 0600, outside the repository)
# The traditional IRA account's IBKR account number: the file its adapter
# (ti-adapter@trad-ira.service, which reads the line TI_ADAPTER_ACCOUNT_KEY
# names in engines/trad-ira.env) and its Flex reader (ti-flex@trad-ira.service)
# are handed (systemd LoadCredential), read from $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/account.
# Names only here; the owner fills the value on the server as KEY=VALUE, with
# no quotes and no spaces. Left empty, each refuses it, naming this line.
# For this account's own IBKR login, add TI_IBKR_FLEX_TOKEN and
# TI_IBKR_FLEX_QUERY_ID here, plus TI_IBKR_FLEX_TRADES_QUERY_ID for executions
# proof, not in secrets.env (docs/manual/reconciliation.md, "What you set up once").
# All Flex values must belong to this login. The trades line may be omitted;
# any present Flex line must be filled in, with no duplicates, quotes or spaces.
# Any line naming TI_IBKR_FLEX that is not exactly one of these keys is refused.
# Without them the IRA's reader refuses: it never uses secrets.env's token.
# The adapter is handed this whole file but reads only IBKR_ACCOUNT_TRAD_IRA.
IBKR_ACCOUNT_TRAD_IRA=
